The roller keeps itself: troves/kiosk-screen, kept by bay 1's pool pass

Editing bay 1 drives the rolling TV the way kiosk-1 keeps its panels: Edge in
kiosk mode, fullscreen, a profile of its own, put back when it goes missing.
No service: the pool's five-minute task runs one `keep` per pass.

- [x] troves/kiosk-screen/screen.ps1: status | keep | on | off | reset
  - finds the instrument by EDID (instrument.yml `match: product`), never the display number
  - no match: nothing shown, and our own browser closed if Windows piled it elsewhere
  - source: the depot's wall when 10.209.1.1:445 answers, else a local render
    of the wall from the mirror's door.py (Autumn, 2026-09-27)
  - stops by process id, never by name (GRANTS)
- [x] troves/kiosk-screen/render.py: wall_files() to the trove's prefix, whole or not at all
- [x] pool.ps1 pass calls `keep roller-tv` from the mirror
- [x] fcpm screen [status|on|off|reset]
- [x] followed on the roller, 2026-09-27: keep (launched), keep (ok, left alone),
      off, keep while off (stays off), on (launched), status
- [x] READMEs: troves table, the trove's own, instruments, the bay's AGENTS.md
- [x] class mode: `fcpm screen class [light]` / `fcpm screen wall`, held in a `page` file;
      followed on the roller 2026-09-27 (sample class, dark)
- [ ] after merge: `fcpm install` (Autumn) so ~/code/bin/pool.ps1 carries the Screens step
- [ ] not followed: the TV unplugged (absent) and the depot answering

Open: the local render has no bookings (the M365 key is kiosk-1's) and no depot
files, so Studio shows bookings.sample.yml, pills marked Sample, and Files is empty.
